    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/01/new-balance-fresh-foam-x-880-v15-review.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The 880 v15 moves to a maximal 40.5/34.5 mm stack with a slightly compliant but notably firm Fresh Foam X feel, giving solid underfoot protection for easy/long miles rather than a plush-soft ride; heel bevel feels a bit clunky early, and the forefoot is stiff/non-flexible.",
        "Responsiveness: The midsole is described as slower-responding with limited bounce/snappiness, so the shoe performs best at easy efforts and not for faster paces.",
        "Stability: It rides as a stable-neutral trainer via a wide platform (especially midfoot), moderate rearfoot sidewalls, mild medial/lateral flare, and a stiff rockered forefoot; heel counter is stiff and straight-line lockdown is good once laced, though lateral movement can feel mildly loose.",
        "Durability: After ~40 miles, foam consistency remains mostly intact with only slight break-in, but visible abrasion is already present on outsole rubber and exposed midsole, indicating average overall mileage/longevity."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2025/01/new-balance-fresh-foam-x-880-v15-multi.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The v15 adds foam at both ends (+3 mm heel, +5 mm forefoot; 40.5/34.5 mm stack), delivering a more cushioned and protective ride, though Fresh Foam X is described as cushioned but still relatively firm.",
        "Responsiveness: Testers describe a firm-responsive feel with smooth rocker-driven transitions and a solid/powerful toe-off, but less bounce and energy return than newer supercritical-foam competitors.",
        "Stability: A stiffer midsole and broader heel/midfoot platform support a neutral-but-stable ride with good lockdown/lateral security, while some runners reported slight heel slippage.",
        "Durability: The shoe is repeatedly characterized as a reliable everyday workhorse built for daily mileage; no clear outsole/material breakdown issues were reported in this review, but wet-surface grip was noted as reduced."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/new-balance-fresh-foam-880v15-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The high-stack Fresh Foam X setup (40.5 mm heel / 34.5 mm forefoot) is firmer and denser than expected, giving solid impact protection with just a touch of softness rather than a plush, squishy feel.",
        "Responsiveness: The ride is firm-yet-flexible with modest bounce, comfortable across easy-to-steady paces but not notably snappy or high in energy return.",
        "Stability: A structured platform (firmer foam, rocker geometry), wide forefoot fit, and secure lockdown deliver strong daily-trainer stability and dependable lateral support.",
        "Durability: Updated outsole traction was praised as excellent/sticky, and reviewers repeatedly highlighted strong build quality and expected long mileage from the materials."
      ]
    }
  ],
